  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_022 (RNA-only, PCA, single) achieved 0.485 acc and config_002 (multimodal, PCA, ViT-L, concat, single) achieved 0.535 acc, confirming that adding an image modality with PCA RNA helps. However, we have no information on whether the RNA encoder choice matters—PCA is a simple linear baseline, and a learned representation like scgpt could capture nonlinear biological structure. Question: config_004 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scgpt while holding everything else identical to config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion). This is a clean single-variable A/B comparison that isolates the RNA representation effect. Why best next: With only 2 experiments done, the RNA encoder is the largest untested design axis that could substantially shift performance. A clean comparison to config_002 will tell us whether learned RNA encoders are worth pursuing, directly guiding whether subsequent experiments should focus on scgpt/scvi variants or whether PCA suffices. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

